@plane z=0 label="Context"
The spec stays `specs/cmd_merge/cmd_merge.spec.md`.

Implements the `specsync merge` command. Auto-resolves git merge conflicts in spec files, flagging files that need manual resolution.

This plane is context. Later planes are lessons, in the order they were learned.
`context.md` stays beside this file.

@plane z=1 label="Key Decisions"
- Module follows the standard command pattern: load config, discover specs, delegate to library module, format output, exit
- Spec was created during the 100% coverage push to dogfood spec-sync on its own codebase

@plane z=2 label="Files to Read First"
- `src/commands/merge.rs` — primary source file

@plane z=3 label="Current Status"
Fully implemented and stable. Spec created to achieve 100% file coverage.

@plane z=4 label="Notes"
- This module is part of the command layer — it orchestrates library modules rather than containing domain logic

@plane z=5 label="Lesson (#862)"
`merge --install` is what makes `git merge-tree` call `merge-file`. The attribute lines can be committed; the driver command is local git config and points at this executable, so an upgrade runs `--install` again. Until that config exists, git's ordinary merge still applies.

@plane z=6 label="A root specs directory needs no prefix (#871)"
A `.gitattributes` pattern beginning `./` never matches, and a bare `.` does not disappear when only slashes are trimmed. Normalize both `.` and `./` to an empty directory prefix, then emit `**/*.spec.md` and `**/requirements.md`. Prove the installed behavior with `git check-attr` on root and nested spec and requirements paths for both spellings; comparing generated strings alone would not prove Git selects the driver.
